---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
const toc = [{id:'list',label:'Subprocessors'},{id:'ai',label:'Cloud AI model providers'},{id:'own',label:'Systems we run ourselves'},{id:'changes',label:'Changes and notice'},{id:'contact',label:'Questions'}];
---
<Legal title={'Subprocessors'} eyebrow='Trust' meta='Last updated: October 11, 2026' lede='The third-party providers that help us run Albena and albena.ai, what they do, what data they touch and where.' description='Albena subprocessors: hosting, email, domains and optional cloud AI providers, with purpose, data and region. Unknown regions are marked to be confirmed.' toc={toc}>
<section id="list"><h2>Subprocessors</h2><p>We use a small number of providers. Each is limited to the data its job needs. Where we have not yet confirmed a region we say <strong>to be confirmed</strong> rather than guess. Vendor assurance reports are being collected and are not yet on file, so we do not claim them here.</p>
<div class="tbl"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Data involved</th><th scope="col">Region</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td><td>Website and customer portal hosting (Workers), DNS, CDN, TLS and web protection, Turnstile spam check, database and backup storage (D1, R2), email routing and delivery for support and sign-in messages.</td><td>Site traffic and request metadata, form submissions, account and portal data, sign-in and support email.</td><td>Global edge network for serving pages. Portal database and backup storage: Eastern North America. Email processing region: to be confirmed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>GitHub, Inc. (Microsoft)</td><td>Source code hosting and build/test automation (Actions).</td><td>Source code and build secrets. No customer data.</td><td>To be confirmed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>GoDaddy Operating Company, LLC</td><td>Domain registration and renewal.</td><td>Domain registrant contact details. No customer data.</td><td>To be confirmed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stripe, Inc.</td><td>Payment processing and invoices, only for accounts where billing is turned on.</td><td>Billing contact and payment details, which Stripe collects directly. We do not see full card numbers.</td><td>To be confirmed.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="ai"><h2>Cloud AI model providers</h2><p>Albena handles everyday requests on hardware you own. Cloud AI models are <strong>off by default</strong>, and no cloud model provider is enabled for customer data today. If you choose to allow one, Albena tells you what leaves your home. Before any provider is enabled for customer data we will add it here with its purpose, the data it receives and its region (until confirmed, shown as &ldquo;to be confirmed&rdquo;).</p></section>
<section id="own"><h2>Systems we run ourselves</h2><p>Support messages sent to our role mailboxes are turned into tickets in a service-management system that Omar Huertas LLC operates. It is not a third-party subprocessor, but it holds the messages you send us. Its hosting location is to be confirmed.</p></section>
<section id="changes"><h2>Changes and notice</h2><p>We review this list at least once a year and whenever we add or replace a provider. Material changes are shown on this page with a new date, and early-access members are told by email before a new provider receives their personal information. Fonts are served from our own site; no visitor data goes to Google Fonts.</p></section>
<section id="contact"><h2>Questions</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:privacy@albena.ai">privacy@albena.ai</a>. See also the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, the <a href="/security">security page</a> and the <a href="https://status.albena.ai" rel="noopener">status page</a>.</p></section>
</Legal>
